    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.indentscope\n\n### Description\n\nIf you open two windows on the same buffer indentscope highlights on both as you move around. I'm using LazyVim.\r\n\r\nhttps://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1597820/222766656-d58e3140-876a-4636-ab95-7969f7196582.mp4\r\n\r\n\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.8.3\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. `nvim -nu minimal.lua`\r\n2. ...\r\n\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nOnly highlight the active window?\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nHighlighting every window with the same buffer.",
