            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\r\n\r\nUnfortunately, this is impossible with current Neovim capabilities. The reason is that highlighting functionality (as is designed) is done with extended marks (a.k.a extmarks, see `:h extmark`). They are tied to the buffer and there is (currently at least) no way to show them only in some windows. And there seems to be no interest to implement it right now.\r\n\r\nClosing this as there is nothing can be done here before new functionality is added to Neovim.",
